  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed two-bedroom basement dwelling would fail to provide a high quality standard of accommodation for future occupiers. By reason of the reliance on relatively small and enclosed lightwells as the primary source of outlook and natural light  to all principal habitable rooms, together with the complete absence of private amenity space, the development would provide a constrained and poor quality living environment. The proposal would therefore fail to secure satisfactory living conditions for future occupiers and would be contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021), Core Policy 30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD 8, DMD 9 and DMD 37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), and the objectives of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "The proposed development has failed to demonstrate that it would provide a safe form of residential accommodation having regard to the site's identified surface water flood risk. In particular, the introduction of a self-contained basement dwelling containing habitable accommodation has not been shown to be safe from flooding for its lifetime, nor has it been demonstrated that future occupiers could safely access and evacuate the site during a flood event. Furthermore, the proposal fails to incorporate an appropriate surface water drainage strategy or maximise the use of Sustainable Drainage Systems in accordance with the drainage hierarchy. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policy SI13 of the London Plan, Core Policy CP28 of the Enfield Core Strategy, Policies DMD60 and DMD61 of the Enfield Development Management Document and the flood risk and climate resilience objectives of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "The proposed development fails to demonstrate that the site frontage can satisfactorily accommodate the proposed parking provision whilst also providing safe and convenient pedestrian access, adequate cycle parking, refuse and recycling storage and appropriate landscaping. The submitted layout has not demonstrated that vehicles could safely and independently access and manoeuvre within the site, nor that the various frontage requirements associated with the development can coexist without conflict. The proposal would therefore result in an unsatisfactory frontage arrangement to the detriment of highway safety and sustainable transport objectives, contrary to Policy T6 of the London Plan and Policies DMD45 and DMD47 of the Enfield Development Management Document."
  ],
